<h3><a href="monstereditor">The Monster Editor</a></h3>

<p>The monster editor will allow you to modify the database of monsters as well as all of their stats. You can also edit the
monster information and delete them as needed.</p>

<h3><a href="monstereditorregex">The Page Parser</a></h3>

<p>This will allow you to copy pages from the monster manual and automatically get monster stats. You will just need to have
some text to copy into via a PDF or similar tool then paste it inside the input box and let the RegEx do it's magic.</p>

<h3><a href="encountereditor">The Encounter Editor</a></h3>

<p>The encounter editor allows you to create combat encounters. Within these encounters you can include a description of what 
the encounter is about. You can also add and remove monsters that are created with the monster editor to the encounter with
the click of a button.</p>

<h3>Learn More About Dungeons and Dragons</h3>

<p>If you are new to D&D then <a target="_blank" href="https://www.dndbeyond.com/sources/dnd/free-rules/playing-the-game#TheSixAbilities">DnD Beyond</a> is a good place to start when learning about the system.</p>
<p>If you want to use the Page Parsing tool you can use the monster section on <a target="_blank" href="https://www.dndbeyond.com/monsters">DnD Beyond</a> to pull any of the stat blocks you need.</p>